#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087475 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/id #uuid "73491cdd-3c8c-5203-b403-6176f6eb2917" :question/math-academy-id "e-5280" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z$, shown in the following Argand diagram, in exponential form.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/898/Source/Images/a0fe46e109e3784d66675d033d5fdbd8.png)" :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= x + \\textrm{i}y \\\\\n&=-3 + 2\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form\n\n$$\nz = r\\textrm{e}^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nr= \\mid z \\mid\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arg(z)\n$$\n\nwe first calculate $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr = \\mid z \\mid &= \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-3)^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\arg (z) &= π - \\mid \\arctan (\\frac{y}{x}) \\mid \\\\\n&= π - \\mid \\arctan (\\frac{2}{3}) \\mid \\\\\n&= π - 0.588 \\\\\n&= 2.554\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places.\n\nFinally, substituting\n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{13}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta=2.554\n$$\n\ninto\n\n$$\nz=re^{\\textrm{i} \\theta}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\nz = \\sqrt{13}\\,\\textrm{e}^{2.554\\,\\textrm{i}}\\,\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087476 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/id #uuid "339f9406-2f1a-52de-959b-23a7fe73ef68" :question/math-academy-id "e-5282" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=4+4\\textrm{i}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form\n\n$$\nz = r\\textrm{e}^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nr= \\mid z \\mid\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arg(z)\n$$\n\nwe first calculate $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr = \\mid z \\mid &= \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4^{2} + 4^{2}} \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nθ = \\arg (z) &= \\arctan (\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\\n&= \\arctan (1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{π}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting\n\n$$\nr=4\\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\ninto\n\n$$\nz=re^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\nz = 4\\sqrt{2}\\,\\textrm{e}^{\\pi\\textrm{i}/4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "099f0768-b014-55cb-b63b-f7d85b833073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.463\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266049} {:answer/id #uuid "7d180bc9-48d4-52b0-a142-7e634cdda919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.281\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266050} {:answer/id #uuid "1beab5ef-a033-5ba1-a636-839356156fd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.974\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266051} {:answer/id #uuid "5a62b093-64a7-58f2-8818-0e03ab067f8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.281\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266052} {:answer/id #uuid "9644d12d-871f-59c2-8a4b-3ddc88f4b08c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.463\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9644d12d-871f-59c2-8a4b-3ddc88f4b08c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.463\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266053} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ce2e21-bef8-5bb3-9b61-46e5fc5afa8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266048}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8f53ade-50ac-5107-884e-6acc18d8661f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107425" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-3-\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-1}{-3})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{3})| \\\\  & ≈3.463.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =3.463$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.463\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12c6b7a2-592f-5ec7-b33b-3d0055bd9ced" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266056} {:answer/id #uuid "2ed57aa9-89fa-5e52-abd7-cae9681035e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=3\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266057} {:answer/id #uuid "ee82e9ad-534d-57e2-9e3e-61347468e97b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=3\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266058} {:answer/id #uuid "e6578901-50b6-5f6c-9626-0461d3bf47a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266059} {:answer/id #uuid "cd50944c-0faf-507a-99ec-2dbd52517f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd50944c-0faf-507a-99ec-2dbd52517f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266060} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e89bc8d-3db1-5bf4-9dad-36f962d99483" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266055}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd5f7e02-06fb-58a5-8972-0a228aeaf734" :question/math-academy-id "q-107427" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953226/assets/7b72c7db59c20e5b3a86cde6b212cfdd88204588d0e5cca29524ba485aee5346.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the first quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58b3d4e1-b419-5c68-9f70-67ede4505082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266063} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9fb541-9791-5b91-9543-760cddbc25d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.429\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266064} {:answer/id #uuid "56be56fd-0b85-52e4-846f-acd7baa06cd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.249\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266065} {:answer/id #uuid "4536e8bf-0ea7-5a49-9a32-d4313fa305a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.249\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266066} {:answer/id #uuid "417b4481-a471-5263-97cd-2a97507b9bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.249\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56be56fd-0b85-52e4-846f-acd7baa06cd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.249\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266065} :answer-field/id #uuid "1501bd7a-f354-5e48-8fba-2ed39fca47df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266062}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d06b3ba1-cbb4-5f0c-b329-9ccba585ef58" :question/math-academy-id "q-17515" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953226/assets/ce8c8d74a7597f04300bf0094826c8245bbd98c45fe8521fec60bada68534f92.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =1+3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the first quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3) \\\\  & ≈1.249.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =1.249$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.249\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57c2bcab-e744-5a4b-8489-8cf154671424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.678\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266070} {:answer/id #uuid "aadc8065-9262-5aba-86ce-9f6e6a2d693e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266071} {:answer/id #uuid "f30c78cc-e2d5-58b7-9d32-e110c1980847" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.786\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266072} {:answer/id #uuid "b4de483b-4e22-565a-b49e-76bef70c2fc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266073} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9ad71e-c59f-51f0-a0e7-516d8e3e7c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.678\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57c2bcab-e744-5a4b-8489-8cf154671424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.678\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266070} :answer-field/id #uuid "a15165f2-6ac4-5c98-bbcc-f3db2b1379fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266069}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3591f83e-e67c-5eb3-b605-9d55afdbddca" :question/math-academy-id "q-17521" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-4+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})| \\\\  & ≈2.678.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =2.678$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.678\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaa51c64-ec76-5069-8aa8-70ab4a996d77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266077} {:answer/id #uuid "2f572805-2e17-5000-b52c-9cbc56ef2476" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266078} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b7df6a-1745-5274-892f-3ed28913d5e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266079} {:answer/id #uuid "c4312907-9b06-51a0-8298-475a6b0a3e26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266080} {:answer/id #uuid "59576f99-c7e2-5c45-a386-3535945a48e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f572805-2e17-5000-b52c-9cbc56ef2476" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266078} :answer-field/id #uuid "f30eda78-02c2-5957-a436-8bcb280f7bf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266076}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f23dfcc9-b6fc-590c-98c4-5afd18cc88c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-17523" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-3-3\\text{i}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the third quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-3}{-3})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=3\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e196a07-e8ac-5e3a-a250-6e0f630f4f17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266084} {:answer/id #uuid "db4886a7-3e24-53ab-af4b-13c10e5a3e0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266085} {:answer/id #uuid "24957ce5-8bef-5313-a273-c3fd887c263b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266086} {:answer/id #uuid "a53a9014-4a0f-5e2c-9e91-a0fea618c8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266087} {:answer/id #uuid "af6e13b1-5b52-5751-beef-3e5aecd92e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=4\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a53a9014-4a0f-5e2c-9e91-a0fea618c8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266087} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a506ad3-c623-5a2a-8379-b31eb74e3745" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266083}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f04f4ac-0cb3-59fe-b7b9-4fd4996a151f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71972" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953226/assets/a0d3f6646cb3a1faa99ba07e76956faf9be1c6f117191c539aae63e3fc1a2ee1.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =2+2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the first quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "882c5678-2512-5834-bede-44d5d57e2929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{4\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266091} {:answer/id #uuid "32f80951-1ca9-55fa-8461-abefdfe13f77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266092} {:answer/id #uuid "be0ae716-72fc-5a6c-8368-4065f6f09a15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266093} {:answer/id #uuid "d9e9ad04-8e4e-5307-8ff0-289448f1641b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266094} {:answer/id #uuid "898583d2-0c21-5b35-af91-c6d4035519d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be0ae716-72fc-5a6c-8368-4065f6f09a15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266093} :answer-field/id #uuid "857ae680-d64d-527d-9d2e-2e387fa05586" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266090}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3b9ffd2-cfe1-5d86-a039-ea56ef371506" :question/math-academy-id "q-71981" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-\\sqrt{3}-\\text{i}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the third quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-1}{-\\sqrt{3}})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\text{i}/6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c49e3d4-1141-5e86-9dc0-07a769f8d693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266098} {:answer/id #uuid "6b55a12f-e52a-5d98-84d6-20878083f7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.338\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266099} {:answer/id #uuid "32aa2e4b-9f77-5cb7-8958-e69543136db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.989\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266100} {:answer/id #uuid "4c394217-aa5e-5f73-8b5a-b6cc3654b8ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266101} {:answer/id #uuid "f92c6ec2-5174-5770-b4fe-0716b26824e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.338\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c49e3d4-1141-5e86-9dc0-07a769f8d693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266098} :answer-field/id #uuid "e293d670-8dd1-5590-974c-860db0453b5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266097}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de095b2a-fbb0-51f2-b405-5336c443d2b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-8076" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=5-\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-1}{5})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{5})| \\\\  & ≈2\\pi -0.197\\,39… \\\\  & ≈6.086.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{26}$ and $\\theta =6.086$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266103 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca13b29b-a033-5f4e-86c7-b8d0a5b90dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\,\\text{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266105} {:answer/id #uuid "0a41bfef-21b2-5d19-8981-a7ed296506d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.678\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266106} {:answer/id #uuid "84de1573-a25d-5301-8ac3-6ff3f8f34a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.605\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266107} {:answer/id #uuid "e0944585-b9b9-5a31-b54a-39887fcc57cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.605\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266108} {:answer/id #uuid "ec4a3bd8-9019-5e67-9887-ecc6ccede109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.678\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0944585-b9b9-5a31-b54a-39887fcc57cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.605\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266108} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d356167-4418-5678-b3f0-a868c81f9ca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266104}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7d92c47-1d38-5eb0-92d8-d988373605fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-8082" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953226/assets/18dd1668d0e9eaeb1be7919821707bbf1d472b22b00acf68a921a3522b2f5f7f.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-4-2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the third quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-2}{-4})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})| \\\\  & ≈\\pi +0.463\\,64… \\\\  & ≈3.605.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =3.605$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.605\\,\\text{i}}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "178963aa-5fc4-5b26-a28c-3f4b2abddcc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.859\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266112} {:answer/id #uuid "b5da35b5-3317-5823-bebf-1d2ec8790210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.983\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266113} {:answer/id #uuid "c960c523-91b5-5431-ac21-c321428e148d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{11}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266114} {:answer/id #uuid "5869d2b5-1000-5095-bcb1-0f15ad0a9a05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.983\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266115} {:answer/id #uuid "b6f2ceb3-9580-528a-b384-a4d5f208ac0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.159\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6f2ceb3-9580-528a-b384-a4d5f208ac0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.159\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266116} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7a958f8-baab-5993-91b6-96ce675043fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266111}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "786f2ec5-3904-5211-975b-9f7327fe00cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-8084" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953226/assets/a4066e842d7b94527aedd124c113ac9fd0b0f444d0d46152c5794c6f4d022074.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-2+3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{3}{2})| \\\\  & ≈2.159.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{13}$ and $\\theta =2.159$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.159\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}]}
